From d1577adb8821f9d2b1ffba59cb3a5b74b7b032ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asahi Lina <lina@asahilina.net>
Date: Thu, 18 Aug 2022 02:13:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rust: soc: apple: rtkit: Add Apple RTKit abstraction

RTKit is Apple's proprietary real-time operating system framework, used
across many subdevices on Apple Silicon platforms including NVMe, system
management, GPU, etc. Add Rust abstractions for this subsystem, so that
it can be used by upcoming Rust drivers.

Signed-off-by: Asahi Lina <lina@asahilina.net>
[Youwes09: reworked for lifetime-bound drivers: the handler lives in a
 pinned Registration tied to the bound device, like irq::Registration,
 and callbacks get the RtKit to reply through; shared buffers and early
 messages left out until a driver uses them; re-export the SoC bus items
 from kernel::soc, which the rust_soc sample uses; the Kconfig symbol
 depends on a built-in RTKit, as the Rust phylib abstractions do]
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
